(a) Every applicant for a license under this chapter shall make written application to the city manager on forms furnished by the city. The applicant shall answer all questions on the application truthfully, under oath, and shall supply all information and furnish all certificates, affidavits, bonds and other supporting data or documents as required by this chapter. No application shall be deemed complete unless accompanied by all required documentation, a set of the applicant(s)' fingerprints, which shall be promptly submitted to the Georgia Bureau of Investigation, pursuant to O.C.G.A. § 3-3-2(c), and payment of the requisite fees. Required documentation includes, but is not limited to, the following:
(1) Initial/renewal application on form(s) provided by the city;
(2) Business entity information affidavit;
(3) Licensee oath and affirmation statement;
(4) Licensee investigation authorization and privacy statement acknowledgment;
(5) Applicant(s) fingerprints;
(6) Planning and zoning compliance certification from planning & development services, including a certificate of occupancy or certificate of completion, as applicable, and fire marshal statement as to use, occupancy type, capacity, and sufficiency of fire suppression system(s);
(7) Certification of compliance with security camera system requirements of this chapter from City of Griffin Chief of Police, or designee, as applicable;
(8) Balance sheet of proposed capitalization of business and its source;
(9) Sworn inventory statement, as applicable;
(10) Current scale drawing of premises as required by section 6-35 of this chapter;
(11) Real property owner information and lease, as applicable;
(12) Copies of all ATT-17 Personnel Statements provided to the state;
(13) Articles of incorporation or organization, operating agreements, or other business organization documents, as applicable;
(14) All other records, documents, information, or data as may be requested by the city manager, chief of police, or other city officer or designee.
(b) Each application shall state the name and address of each applicant; the place where the proposed business is to be located; and the type(s) of license(s) applied for. The application shall also contain a beginning balance sheet showing the proposed original capitalization of the business and its source. If an applicant is a corporation or other business entity, the application shall state the names of all officers and owners of the entity and the percentage ownership of each. If the applicant is a partnership, the application shall state the names of all partners therein, whether general or limited. All applications shall include the names of all persons that have or will have a direct or indirect beneficial interest in the business for which the license is sought. Each application shall also contain such additional information as the city manager prescribes, shall be verified as true by the applicant before a notary public, and shall be accompanied by payment of the requisite fee(s) for the type(s) of license(s) applied for. All license fees include a nonrefundable application fee of $150.00 to cover the cost of investigating the applicant and processing the application. If the application is denied, the license fee paid when the application was submitted shall be refunded less the nonrefundable application fee.
(Ord. No. 25-005, § 1, 5-27-2025)

